author: codex
close_reason: "Superseded by feature pm-jira-i7fd (2026-06-03 enhancement sweep). Delivered the overlapping goals offline-testable in this session: capability correctness, --assignee + richer filters, field-mapping depth, validate diagnostics, dry-run no-network, opt-in export-on-write hook. Idempotent re-import + live backoff deferred (see child tasks) as they need live creds / a larger refactor."
body: "Deepen pm-jira to domain-appropriate maximum against SDK 2026.5.31.\n\nVALUE: pm-jira already had jira sync/import/export + schema fields + status-map (commit dbf38cf). This feature closes the remaining real gaps from the enhancement brief.\n\nOUTCOME: idempotent re-import (update existing pm items matched on Jira key instead of duplicating; persist jira_key/jira_url), a real credential+reachability preflight surfaced as the 'preflight' capability, rate-limit/backoff robustness, and an --assignee filter. Manifest capabilities corrected to match what is actually registered (drop unregistered 'services' filler; add 'preflight').\n\nACCEPTANCE CRITERIA:\n- pm jira import re-run updates matched items (no duplicates), keyed on Jira key provenance + jira_key field.\n- jira_key/jira_url persisted onto items (via pm update --field or description marker fallback).\n- pm jira preflight validates creds + base URL + reachability with clear failure_hints; registerPreflight guard registered.\n- 429/503 responses retried with exponential backoff + Retry-After honoring.\n- --assignee filter augments default JQL.\n- manifest capabilities == registered surfaces exactly.\n- typecheck/build/test/changelog:check/release:check all green; new unit tests for idempotency match + backoff parse + preflight.\n- Functionally tested in --dry-run against scratch workspace with fixture JSON."
